{
  "requirement": "Each page has the same result fields as the originating tool. Text reads return\nsuccessive portions of text. Listings, outlines, and searches return successive\narrays of whole entries in their original order. Only a page with a successor\nincludes `next`.\n\nReusing a UUID returns the same page from the original snapshot, including the\nsame successor UUID if more remains. A malformed UUID, an unknown UUID, or a UUID\nfrom another conversation returns a tool error under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.tool_agent.isolation`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover every obligation in `pages.behavior`. The isolation citation (`tool_agent.isolation`) is covered by the foreign-conversation tests. I read the paging implementation (`Pages::prepare`, `Pages::search` and `Pages::get` in `agent/pages.rs`) only to see which paths share code.\n\n**Obligations and tests**\n- **Same result fields as the originating tool**\n  - Search: `search_pages_return_every_original_match_in_order` asserts `complete`, a parseable `search_id`, `instructions` only on the first page, and each entry exactly as `{node, excerpt, tag}`.\n  - Outline: `outline_continuations_keep_the_file_and_complete_ordered_items` asserts `node` on every page.\n  - Source read: `source_read_pages_retain_text_and_dependencies_without_another_read` asserts `node.selector` on later pages.\n  - Graph read: `read_node` has only the `text` field (`metadata` is `{}`), and the graph read pages test checks `text` on each page.\n- **Text reads return successive portions**\n  - `graph_read_pages_retain_the_prepared_snapshot_after_contents_change` uses multibyte text and asserts that the concatenated pages equal the original after the content changed.\n  - `source_read_pages_retain_text_and_dependencies_without_another_read` does the same for source reads.\n- **Listings, outlines and searches return successive arrays of whole entries in original order**\n  - Listing: `listing_continuations_return_complete_paths_from_the_original_listing` uses 2000 files and a file added mid-paging, and asserts the full ordered list.\n  - Outline: the outline test asserts 401 items in order, with the right nodes and kinds.\n  - Search: the search test covers 350 matches across pages, checking order, the exact entry on each page, and the total count.\n- **Only a page with a successor includes `next`**\n  - The graph read pages test asserts `next` is present only on index 0.\n  - The search test stops on the page without `next`.\n  - `source_tools_forward_arguments_and_present_discovery_and_read_results` asserts `next` is absent on a single-page result.\n  - The loops in the listing, outline and source read tests end exactly when `next` is absent.\n- **Reusing a UUID returns the same page and successor**\n  - `search_obligations_follow_delivery_and_keep_the_original_snapshot` replays `get_next_page` after the file changed on disk and asserts the same text (so the same successor).\n  - That test also asserts `get_next_page` is idempotent when called again after the finish calls.\n  - `Pages::get` is the single shared lookup, and it serves both `retained` paths (search and prepare). The reuse test therefore exercises the shared behavior. Listing, outline and text reads have no separate reuse test, but they use the same lookup.\n- **Original snapshot**\n  - Every paging test mutates the underlying source or contents after the first page and still gets the original data.\n- **Malformed UUID, unknown UUID, or UUID from another conversation returns a tool error**\n  - Malformed and unknown: the outline test dispatches `get_next_page` with `\"invalid\"` and an all-zero UUID, and asserts both are errors.\n  - Another conversation (search): the search test asserts that `peer.dispatch(\"get_next_page\", &next)` is an error.\n  - Another conversation (read pages): `graph_page_ids_from_a_populated_peer_conversation_are_rejected` has a populated peer, a distinct page UUID, and asserts an `is_error` result containing \"unknown page\".\n\n**Discovery pages and dependencies**\n- `source_discovery_and_its_pages_do_not_register_reads` checks that pages never record observations. This is outside `pages.behavior`, but it is consistent with it.\n\n**Conclusion**\n\nI found no gap: each clause has a test that exercises it and asserts the outcome. The tests carry `{test}` references to the subject. There are no acknowledgments to assess.",
  "references": "1ac80069e6c37d2808f2a07935fa541926528e3931df8b3a2c423e0fed2a9800",
